# Ruby Conventions

- RuboCop (150 char max line length)
- Compact `module/class` definitions — `class Foo::Bar`, not nested `module Foo; class Bar`
- Models: validate presence/uniqueness and add appropriate indexes
- Database foreign keys: prefer associations/callbacks unless a constraint is needed; assess delete behavior and production migration/locking risk first
- Controllers: strong params, authorization and request-boundary validation (`422` for malformed input)

## Specs

- Prefer `with_modified_env` over stubbing `ENV`
- Parallel/reloading envs: compare `error.class.name`, not constant class equality
- Prefer `let` and direct per-example setup over one-use helper methods
